{"resourceIdentifier":"3812","resourceName":"Painted Forest Carbon Project","description":"The Painted Forest Carbon Project creates GHG offsets and forest health benefits through the purchase and management of 59,846 ha (147,882 acres) of private forest land, located in the District of Algoma near Sault Ste. Marie, Ontario, Canada. The property is in a unique geographic location that will contribute to landscape level forest connectivity between the already established Lake Superior Provincial Park and Algoma Headwaters Provincial Park. The project avoids GHG emissions that would occur from harvesting the existing forestland. In the project scenario, significant carbon stocks are retained and sequestered through the preservation and continuing growth of the forest, creating substantial net benefits for Ontarians, and providing biodiversity benefits from the conservation and management of the area’s forest ecosystem.\r\n\r\nThe project scenario is improved forest management, wherein PFLP undertakes the forest carbon project and associated ecosystem protection and enhancement activities. The project scenario includes a low level of timber harvesting as part of forest management activities for the purposes of forest health, incidental infrastructure, ecosystem resilience, biodiversity and other conservation objectives.","location":{"latitude":47.187006,"longitude":-84.252531},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2022-10-31","endExclusive":"2022-12-01","endInclusive":"2022-11-30"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"3812"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"ON"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Perimeter Forest Limited Partnership"},{"type":"string","value":"ON, Canada"},{"type":"string","value":"6472227101"},{"type":"string","value":"cpittman@perimeterforest.com"}]},{"code":"PRO